Navigation configuration
------------------------
The following files were reconstructed offline on 2026-10-13 from documented
parameter interfaces and the accepted RobotOps tuning values:

  ros2_ws/src/robot_navigation/config/navigation.yaml
  ros2_ws/src/robot_navigation/config/localization.yaml
  ros2_ws/src/robot_navigation/config/profiles/navfn_rpp.yaml
  ros2_ws/src/robot_navigation/config/profiles/smac_dwb.yaml
  ros2_ws/src/robot_navigation/config/slam.yaml

Their newly authored configuration and comments are Apache-2.0 RobotOps source.
No upstream implementation, example prose or example configuration block was
incorporated in the reconstruction. API names, plugin identifiers, parameter
values and order-sensitive lists preserve the existing operational contract.

Historical versions remain in Git with unresolved authorship. Prior NOTICE
references to Nav2 examples and SLAM Toolbox identify possible relationships,
not a proven source chain. The historical DWB critic block matches a Nav2 Humble
example; that does not establish its actual origin or clear historical rights.
The reconstruction does not retroactively license those versions.

Interface references (not bundled implementation):
  Nav2 / navigation2: https://github.com/ros-navigation/navigation2
  SLAM Toolbox: https://github.com/SteveMacenski/slam_toolbox

See docs/CONFIGURATION_PROVENANCE.md for pinned references, file-specific licence
observations, reconstruction scope and unchanged semantic identities.

Dependencies
------------
RobotOps builds against, but does not include, ROS 2, Nav2, SLAM Toolbox,
Gazebo, ros2_control and npm/PyPI packages. Their own licenses apply. Nav2 has
Apache, BSD and LGPL files; its repository is not uniformly Apache-2.0.
SLAM Toolbox declares LGPL at package level, but inspected implementation files
also contain non-specific CCPL headers. No such implementation is redistributed
here. Setting its parameter interfaces does not import implementation text.
The robot_navigation slam_runner links the installed SLAM Toolbox library;
compiled binaries or container distributions require a separate dependency
licence/compliance review, including LGPL obligations and header discrepancies.

